  "final_message": "I have run git status to check the repository state. I will proceed as soon as the command completes.\nI have listed the test directory to check existing test coverage. I will proceed as soon as the command completes.\nI have run a command to list all source files. I will proceed as soon as it completes.\nI have run git log to check previous commit changes. I will proceed as soon as it completes.\nI am running the unit tests to verify the baseline status. I will proceed as soon as it completes.\nI have scheduled a check for the running test task and will proceed when notified.\nI am waiting for the unit tests to finish running.\nI will now wait for the test run to finish.\nI have searched for any existing deprecation patterns in the codebase and will proceed when the search finishes.\nI cannot remove the `channel` field from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model due to architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/GEMINI.md):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Key Considerations\n\n1. **External Contract Compatibility**: Removing `channel` from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event schema is a breaking, non-additive change that would break deployed consumers in `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`.\n2. **Model Dependency**: [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) constructs [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) from the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) entity. As long as the published event requires `channel`, the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model and [`NewOrder`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/order.ts#L32-L38) input must retain it.\n3. **Deprecation Process**: Any retirement of `channel` must go through a formal deprecation cycle across downstream consumer repositories before removal.\n",
